      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Look for candidates who speak with a measured cadence, using precise, high-level vocabulary without resorting to jargon that sounds forced. Their body language should be open yet contained—confident posture, steady eye contact, and minimal distracting fidgeting. The \"vibe\" you want is one of quiet assurance; they don't need to shout to be heard, which is often the hallmark of true, established authority.",
      "source": "target",
